  "note": "Test 48, an integration revoke and per-effect counting (I.5.8; decision 8's amendment: revocation_applied at a host's first applied or duplicate for the revocation, naming that record). Astation's native revoke M1_revoke reaches the feed first and host-d applies it; nothing is reported until the Station records its own revoke S4_revoke (the Portal revoked the integration, covering host-b, host-c and host-d), which reports host-d at once, naming M1. host-b applies S4: one revocation_applied. The Station re-signs it as S5_revoke_interrupt, which adds interrupt_running: true; host-b reports it duplicate for the revocation and applied for the interrupt, and nothing more is reported for host-b. An ack claiming host-c on host-b's link is refused whole (the ack's claim must be the link's association). host-c applied the revocation through another record first (a native revoke in another Station's feed it syncs) and reports S4 duplicate: that counts, and its revocation_applied names S4. revoked{all_applied} follows, delivered only after every covered host's revocation_applied is confirmed: reports of one principal go in the order they were made, one at a time. Record times are the vectors'; the order is the feed's.",
